config.prompt:
You are the project controls lead on the Kestrel Vale Bypass, a 9.5 km highway realignment baselined at a planned duration (PD) of 10 months. Cumulative planned value (PV), in thousands: month 1 = 400; 2 = 900; 3 = 1500; 4 = 2300; 5 = 3200; 6 = 4200; 7 = 5200; 8 = 6000; 9 = 6600; 10 = 7000.

Status is at actual time AT = 6 months. The dashboard reports cumulative earned value of 3000, but 250 of that is a drainage realignment variation whose change request was REJECTED by the change board — exclude it before any analysis.

Using the corrected cumulative earned value, compute:
1. es — earned schedule ES, interpolating linearly between the two plan months the corrected EV falls between (months, 2 decimal places);
2. sv_time — SV(t) = ES - AT (months, 2 decimal places);
3. spi_time — SPI(t) = ES / AT (2 decimal places);
4. eac_time — EAC(t) = PD / SPI(t) (months, 2 decimal places).
